 "result": "[notifications-service#Delivery and retries] (score 0.79)\nNotificationsService: Delivery and retries\nIts retry semantics are three attempts with a 250ms backoff, configured by RETRY_ATTEMPTS. A message that fails all three attempts moves to the dead-letter list, and the caller is not told. Callers that need confirmation poll the message status.\n\n[notifications-service#Overview] (score 0.73)\nNotificationsService: Overview\nNotificationsService exposes the NotificationsAPI. Any service that needs to send an email, an SMS, or a push message hands it to this API instead of talking to a provider directly.\n\n[payments-service#Integrations] (score 0.70)\nPaymentsService: Integrations\nIt calls the NotificationsAPI on a declined authorization, so the customer hears about a decline even when checkout has already returned.\n\nPaymentsService is maintained by the same team as BillingService."
}

